## 🔍 Evaluating Severity

* List / Read Only: If you can only list files, this is typically closed as Informational or Low severity unless sensitive personal data or source code is exposed (CSS files are publicly viewable by design).
* Write Permissions: If you can upload or overwrite files (like the existing .css.gz files), this constitutes a Critical / High vulnerability (Stored XSS / Defacement potential) and qualifies for a significant bounty according to the rules table.

